.TH EUCLID-CLI-ESS-DELETE-SECRET 1 "September 2026" "euclid-cli 1.0.53" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ess-delete-secret \- delete a secret
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli ess delete-secret
.BR \-\-name | \-n
.I NAME
.SH DESCRIPTION
Deletes a secret and the value it holds, immediately and for good.
.PP
Unlike
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-delete-key (1),
there is no grace period. A key is what protects other things, so
deleting one is delayed to leave time to migrate off it; a secret is
the thing itself, so there would be nothing left to recover afterwards
and nothing a delay could save.
.PP
Whatever was using the secret will fail to read it on its next attempt.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-name " " \fINAME\fR
Secret name, within the caller's own account and namespace. Required.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The secret was deleted; its name and ERN are printed as JSON.
.TP
.B 1
No secret of that name exists, the caller was not granted it, or the
server could not be reached.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli-ess (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ess-list-secrets (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-delete-key (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Jens Vogt <jens.vogt@opitz-consulting.com>
